syntax: parse more zsh expansion operators, arithmetic, and glob groups

These are valid zsh (zshexpn(1), "PARAMETER EXPANSION" and "FILENAME
GENERATION"; zshmisc(1), "ARITHMETIC EVALUATION"; zshmodules(1),
zsh/mathfunc) but were rejected:

	${name::=word}          # assign unconditionally
	${name:/pattern/repl}   # replace only a match of the whole value
	${name:^array}          # zip two arrays
	${name:^^array}         # zip, repeating the shorter array
	$(( #name ))            # code of the first character of $name
	$(( ##a ))              # code of a character, also ##\n, ##^A, ##\M-\C-x
	$(( [#16] x ))          # output base
	$(( sqrt(x) + atan2(y, x) ))
	ls ((a|b)|c)*           # groups which start with or contain groups
	ls *(e:'(( 1 ))':)      # glob qualifiers with ")" in quotes

Reproducer, before this change:

	$ printf 'echo ${x::=word}\n' | shfmt -ln zsh
	<standard input>:1:10: `=` must follow a name
	$ printf 'echo $(( [#16] 255 ))\n' | shfmt -ln zsh
	<standard input>:1:10: `[` must follow a name like a[i]
	$ printf 'echo $(( sqrt(2) ))\n' | shfmt -ln zsh
	<standard input>:1:9: not a valid arithmetic operator: `(`
	$ printf "ls *(e:'(( 1 ))':)\n" | shfmt -ln zsh
	<standard input>:1:15: a command can only contain words and redirects; encountered `)`

The new operators are AssignAlways, ArrayZip and ArrayZipLongest, with
their tokens; Replace gains Whole; UnaryArithm gains the CharCode operator
while ##x is lexed as a literal constant; FlagsArithm gains Brackets for
the output base; and the new FuncArithm node represents a math function
call. A zsh glob qualifier or group is still kept as an opaque literal,
but it now ends at its matching parenthesis, skipping quoted strings. The
expand package implements ::= and the whole-value replacement and
evaluates an expression with an output base; math functions stay
unsupported there, like zsh's other array operators.

token_string.go was regenerated with `go run
golang.org/x/tools/cmd/stringer@v0.52.0 -type token -linecomment
-trimprefix _`, as the pinned v0.38.0 fails with Go 1.27, and
tokens_parse.go with `go run gen_token_parse.go`.

Part of https://github.com/mvdan/sh/issues/120.

